**I am Sunny Patel. I run live SEO training for in-house teams and founders across the UK. Every session uses your own site and your own Search Console data. Prices are fixed per team of up to 8 people: £750 for a half-day workshop, £1,250 for a full day and £2,500 for a six-week programme.**

Every engagement starts with a free 20-minute scoping call.

## What is this SEO training and who is it for?

This is live SEO training for a team or a founder working on a real site. It is not a self-paced SEO course. I teach the methods I use on my own sites. The team applies them to its own pages during the session.

I have done SEO since 2010. I have built over 300 sites and run 44 active test sites. One hundred of my own sites have Google Search Console data. I publish research from that portfolio and use it in the training.

The training is for in-house marketing teams, content writers, developers and small business owners. It is SEO training for staff who know the business but not the search side. Founders who want to learn SEO on their own site can book it one-to-one.

My guide to [in-house SEO versus an agency or consultant](/blog/inhouse-seo-vs-agency-vs-consultant/) compares who should own SEO in a business. Read it before you book if that decision is still open.

## Course, workshop or coaching: which format fits?

Pick a workshop for a team. Pick one-to-one coaching for one person. Pick a course from another provider for a certificate or self-paced study. I do not sell a self-paced course.

| Format | Live time | Best for |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Half-day workshop | 3 hours | A shorter session for a team |
| Full-day workshop | 6 hours | A full SEO training day. The nearest match to a masterclass or bootcamp |
| Six-week team programme | Six weekly 90-minute sessions | Teams that want set work between sessions |
| One-to-one training | 3 or 6 hours | A founder or a single marketer |

Choose a workshop for one live session. Choose the six-week programme when the team wants set work between sessions.

The six-week programme is the closest thing to SEO coaching for a whole team. Each week adds set work and my feedback on it.

## What does the SEO training cover?

The training covers seven modules. I recommend the mix for each booking after the scoping call. Every exercise uses your own site and data.

| Module | What it covers |
| --- | --- |
| Search intent and query mapping | Mapping queries to pages and intent |
| Technical SEO essentials | Crawl, indexation, canonicals, rendering and Core Web Vitals |
| Semantic content and topical maps | Topical maps and page briefs |
| Google Search Console and GA4 | Search Console and GA4 reporting |
| AI search visibility (GEO) | How AI answers use pages |
| Local SEO | Local search |
| WordPress and Shopify | SEO inside the platform the team uses |

Content SEO training is the nearest thing I offer to an SEO copywriting course. It covers briefs, intent and topic coverage rather than sentence style.

I teach AI SEO as tested practice. Nobody can guarantee a citation in an AI answer. The local SEO, WordPress and Shopify modules are added where the team needs them.

The examples come from research I publish:

- a Google update tracker across about 100 sites
- a query-length study of 97 sites: queries of 4 or more words brought 69.8% of clicks
- an experiment register with 11 experiments
- a list of AI referral sources
- a DIY SEO workbook and a migration kit

## In-house and corporate SEO training for teams

In-house training is delivered to one team of up to 8 people at a fixed price. It is bespoke SEO training built on that team's site.

Each fixed price is capped at 8 people. The cap leaves time for each attendee to work through their own examples.

Corporate SEO training follows the same shape. I prepare from your site and your Search Console data. The team works on its own pages during the session. Attendees keep the materials and exercise templates. Sessions can be recorded with the team's agreement.

SEO training for businesses of any size starts with the free scoping call. I then recommend one format and the modules to cover. For a small business team the half-day workshop is the lightest option.

A mixed team can attend one session. Writers, developers and managers work on the same pages.

